WEBVTT

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.190
Amami did?

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:11.800
Yeah.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.130
What's everyone talking about?

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.700
Ah, Inoue!

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.210
What is it?

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.900
We have a stunner! We have a <i>real stunner</i>!

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.450
Our own Amami...

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:25.540
has bought a cell phone!

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.160
What?!

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.920
Wait, what's so shocking about that?

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.890
Well, Amami seems like
she came out of the Meiji era.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.070
I pictured her doing laundry
by hand on a washboard.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.010
Don't insult people so casually!

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.480
It's my first time. I'm kind of nervous.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.840
A pwe-paid... pur-pay...

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.160
Ur?

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:20.070
Urchin!

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:20.870
<i>Urchin?</i>

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.620
Sorry, I'm not used to saying the word.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.450
<i>How did she get "urchin"?</i>

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:31.120
You know, Amami's more suited
to a rotary phone than a cell.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:33.610
The kind with the dial you turn.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.550
How retro do you think she is?

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.710
So why'd you get a cell phone, anyway?

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.850
My dad gave it to me to help me stay safe.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.530
He's always been a worrywart.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.780
Hibiki, be careful!

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:59.650
Remember, if the current
sweeps you away, yell for help!

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.350
Okay!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.990
See you later.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.050
Hibiki, be careful out in the dark!

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.040
Remember, they're always after you!

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:16.960
Okay!

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.160
Really, he's such a worrier.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.430
He has every right to be worried!

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.610
How's a cell phone gonna
keep her safe from them?

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:29.220
Hey, have you bought a strap for it?

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.980
No, not yet...

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.810
Here, you can have one of mine!

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.480
Aren't they cute?

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.310
How about this one?

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.660
This one's great, too!

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.660
Oh, and I'll teach you how to take a selfie.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.160
Thank you.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.330
Hold it up like this...

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.790
Okay, say "cheese!"

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:55.930
It worked!

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.170
And... save...

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.990
What happened? What's in the picture, Ogawa?

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.680
No one will blame you for
deleting that one, Ogawa!

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.740
She's posting it to her blog.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.500
There really is something
in that picture, isn't there?!

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:22.280
Just adding Amami to my contacts
will probably get me some great shots!

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.360
Don't sound so happy about it!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.280
Um...

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:27.700
Inoue.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.330
Y-Yes?

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:33.040
Um... Your number...

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.090
Never mind!

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.510
Want to take a picture together?

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.610
With me?

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.770
You don't want to?

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.100
I don't mind, but...

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.310
Tinkle, tinkle...

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.230
Kitty!

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:04.820
Hey, girlie, looks like ya got somethin' neat there.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:05.610
Yes...

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.700
I'll take a picture with ya.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.120
Really?

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.460
In return, show me your pant—

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.160
What'd ya do that for?!

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.040
The wind just blew it over.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:23.740
You were tryin' to get between me
and my chance to see some panties!

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.610
I had heard rumors of a cat like you,
but I didn't expect you to be <i>this</i> vulgar.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.160
Can it, buzzkill!

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.390
What's wrong with liking panties?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:30.750
Oh, there's the wind picking up again!
What's wrong with liking panties?

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.570
Please, stop it!
Oh, there's the wind picking up again!

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:33.930
Whaaaa—

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.400
It sure is hot today.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.780
And the wet season only just ended.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.910
This heat definitely feels like summer.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.440
I'm so drained...

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.580
And she's melting!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.000
Inoue!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.610
What's with you? Snap out of it!

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.960
There's a tyrant staying at my house.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.800
A tyrant?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.220
My little cousin. He's in elementary school,

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.380
and he's an absolute nightmare.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.100
But at heart, he loves his family.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.660
I have no idea where he gets it from.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.400
<i>He obviously got that attitude from you.</i>

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.720
Is he really that rowdy?

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:24.860
Well, see...

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.660
His name is Yuuki.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.600
Apparently fried eggs are his favorite food,

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.860
so I've been making them for him every day.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.040
But...

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:38.630
Gross! What is this stuff?!
These aren't real fried eggs!

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.540
He says they're gross and
throws them back at me!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.700
I don't want this!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.550
All these eggs are gonna make me fat...

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:51.930
You can have some of my fish.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:52.810
No.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:59.640
I decided I'm gonna do whatever
it takes to get him to like what I cook.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.580
Time to research.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.940
She's really into this.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.200
I wish I could help, since you're so determined,

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.790
but I don't have any free time.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:09.950
I've got work.

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:11.820
Me, too...

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.580
Um, I'm free.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:24.630
Huh?

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:30.990
This is my first time coming to
a friend's house since I transferred.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:33.720
I-It was unavoidable.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:37.060
You're finally home, octopus?

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:43.780
Darn it, Yuuki, I told you to use my name!

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.080
Hello.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.510
I'm Amami Hibiki.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.320
Nice to meet you.

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.980
Sorry about that.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.870
He's a little monster, isn't he?

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.680
It's all right.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:24.180
Wow, you've got good technique.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.400
Thank you.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.360
Let me try...

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:31.770
That's good!

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.030
I'm so glad.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.350
How about these?

00:08:58.580 --> 00:08:59.310
Wrong.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:01.570
They're gross! All wrong!

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:05.560
What are you talking about?
I hate to admit it, but these are delicious!

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.560
Nope, they're gross!

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.250
Why, you...

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.070
I said they're all wrong!

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:10.190
Now, now...
I said they're all wrong!

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.850
How dare you insult

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.500
Lady Amami's

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:19.830
home cooking?!

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.410
Inconceivable!

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.250
Sorry you went to all that trouble.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.960
N-No, I should be apologizing to you.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.650
I'm looking after him

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:44.600
because his dad was in a terrible accident.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.450
They just had the funeral recently...

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.920
And his mom's in the hospital,
about to have a baby.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:01.410
That's why I'd at least like to
give him one little indulgence.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:12.420
I-I'll keep trying to help!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.750
I'll do better next time!

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:25.640
Let's...

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.850
Let's make the best fried eggs ever!

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.570
Wh-What're you getting all worked up over?

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.820
This has nothing to do with you.

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:43.630
You're... You're right.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:49.110
I'm sorry for sticking my nose
where it doesn't belong.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.100
Hey, Inoue.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:11.530
Uehara.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.050
What have we here?

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:17.160
Are you proposing to someone?

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:18.400
It's a get-well gift!

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:21.800
My cousin's mom is in the hospital up the street,

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.330
about to have a baby.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.200
Oh, right, the kid you mentioned.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:31.040
So, how did Amami's fried eggs turn out yesterday?

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:32.600
Well...

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.800
They were good. She really is a great cook.

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:42.730
Guess she's one of those girls whose mom
started to teach her as soon as she could walk.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.010
Actually, I doubt that.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.060
Why's that?

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.640
Yesterday, when we were
talking about her cell phone...

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:57.100
My mother passed away just after I was born.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:59.780
It's always been just my dad and me,

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:03.070
and over the years, he's turned into a real worrier.

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:05.340
That's what she told us.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.170
If it's just her and her dad,

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:11.240
she's probably been doing most
of the cooking for a while now.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:19.200
<i>Then she's been through the
same thing Yuuki's going through.</i>

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:23.510
<i>That's why she...</i>

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.430
<i>And then I...</i>

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:34.090
What? What happened?!

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:44.400
It'll be okay for me to just
learn about frying eggs, right?

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:56.780
The shelves on that side have good stuff, too.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.820
Thank you.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:02.950
Huh?

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.820
We're in here.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:19.800
Twins?!

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.790
Hey, what'cha doin'?

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:30.290
Kitty!

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:36.220
I've been told I can research recipes
on something called the Internet,

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:40.340
so I'm looking for a really
delicious way to fry eggs.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:45.560
I may know a thing or two about frying eggs.

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:46.300
Huh?

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:50.040
Then would you consider teaching me?

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:53.270
Well, now...

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:54.940
All right.

00:13:56.790 --> 00:14:01.030
I'll do it for one flash of your panties a day,
in a wide variety of outfits—

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:06.320
I see.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:09.030
So that's why you want to make delicious fried eggs.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.310
Yes...

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:15.400
But are you sure deliciousness
is what this child truly wants?

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.580
Huh? Well, he said they were gross...

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.260
But he also said they were <i>wrong</i>.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:24.340
Yes...

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:28.850
Then maybe he's comparing them to something?

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:32.720
Something that's no longer there...

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.690
I'm sorry about this, Narumi.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.720
Yuuki's probably driving you crazy.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.830
He has trouble listening.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:47.160
Not really. Nothing I can't handle.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:50.190
Nice try. I can see the exhaustion on your face.

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:57.880
The truth is, no matter how hard I try,

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.210
he calls my fried eggs gross.

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:04.270
Ah, so that's the problem?

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:08.000
It's not your fault, Narumi.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:14.650
Yuuki really loved the fried eggs his dad made.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:17.930
So that's it...

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.750
And did you know this?

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:27.030
My husband learned how to make them
from your grandmother when he was little.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:37.910
Narumi, can you do me a favor?

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.260
<i>I have to tell her.</i>

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.550
<i>But...</i>

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.480
This has nothing to do with you.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.150
Nothing to do with me...

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.710
Hello? This is Amami.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.710
I-It's Inoue...

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:20.800
H-How?

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:23.540
We haven't exchanged numbers—

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.760
I got your number from Uehara.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:32.350
I'm sorry I was so mean last night.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:36.260
I shouldn't have said it
had nothing to do with you.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:39.130
It's okay.

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:46.130
Inoue, there's something
that I think you should know.

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:50.310
Yuuki might not just want his eggs to be tasty.

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:53.370
There may be a certain type he wants.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:59.210
You were still thinking about Yuuki,
even after I was so mean?

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:03.940
W-Well... I just couldn't get it out of my mind...

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:07.760
About that... I was hoping you'd do me a favor.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:09.190
Huh?

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:12.490
She's here, right?

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:13.520
Yes.

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:15.920
Listen, Nana.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:22.710
What Yuuki really wants is
fried eggs the way you made them.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:26.340
So I need you to teach me how to make them.

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:36.110
I see. Keep the seasoning light.

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:39.570
You're supposed to scramble the eggs very gently.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:43.200
Wouldn't this go faster if you did it?

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:48.340
I think your grandmother wants you to learn.

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:52.890
I feel a little bad now.

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:56.620
When she was still with us,

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:01.350
I was too embarrassed to let her teach me

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.540
cooking and all that other girly stuff.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:10.940
I should have just let her teach me...

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:17.370
Um...

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:19.450
Inoue!

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:26.420
You're not gonna complain this time.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.620
This is way too much, octopus!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.900
Shut up and eat!

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.220
Daddy...

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:37.090
Narumi, can you do me a favor?

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:42.870
If Yuuki should start crying,
just let him cry it out.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:46.440
After his father died, he said...

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:51.640
"I can't cry. I'm gonna be a big brother."

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:57.610
He's been holding it in, all this time.

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:14.530
Thanks for everything.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.660
You're cheeky through and through.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.370
Thank you, too, Amami.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:23.090
Oh, no, I didn't do anything.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:24.870
Narumi!

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:24.880
I'm gonna be a big, strong man one day!
Narumi!

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:27.420
I'm gonna be a big, strong man one day!

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:31.420
Yes, yes, do your best.

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.420
Later!

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:46.440
Amami.

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:47.930
Yes?

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:52.950
Um, thanks a bunch, for everything.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:57.090
You're very welcome...

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:00.230
Inoue... Narumi.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.360
Why are you using my full name?

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.880
Using your first name is so new to me.

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:09.900
Just because you normally don't.

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:12.850
I got my name from Nana.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.240
That's wonderful!

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.640
Yeah, yeah, all right, already.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:29.120
Inoue?

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:29.990
Yeah?

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:35.070
Um... Is this how you write "Narumi"?

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.230
Yep, that's it.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:42.810
Your first name's Hibiki, right?

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:44.590
Yes.

00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:58.550
<i>There are so many bonds, in so many places...</i>

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:05.430
<i>And more will be formed tomorrow.</i>

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:43.810
Hey! I'm Yamada Kenta!

00:23:43.810 --> 00:23:46.330
The only guy in the middle of all these girls!

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:47.490
This summer at the beach,

00:23:47.490 --> 00:23:49.580
I'll have all these babes in swimsuits to myself!

00:23:49.580 --> 00:23:52.650
Uehara, I brought everyone's bags!

00:23:52.650 --> 00:23:55.380
Esumi, I reserved the train seats.

00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:58.060
Ogawa, you want this raft inflated, right?

00:23:58.060 --> 00:24:00.710
Whew, it's tough being the man everyone counts on.

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:03.640
Next time on Re-Kan!:
"Summertime Means Beach Time."

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:05.940
Ah, I was buying food and now the train's leaving!

00:24:05.940 --> 00:24:09.180
Wait, guys! Don't ditch me!
